Q. What is Virtualisation?
A:	Virtualization means creating a virtual version of a computer, storage, or network, instead of using physical hardware.
It helps save costs, use resources better, and run multiple systems on one machine. 
Examples: VMware, VirtualBox.

Q. What is Cloud Computing?
A:	Cloud computing means the on-demand delivery of compute, storage, database, and other IT resources and services.
						OR
Cloud Computing is a technology that allows you to store and access data and applications over the internet instead of relying on local computers or personal servers.
Example: Hosting a website on AWS instead of your own server.

Q. Cloud Computing Deployment Models or Types of cloud (Deployment model)?
A: 	☁ Public Cloud – Shared online services (e.g., AWS, Azure).
🏢 Private Cloud – Dedicated to one organization for more control.
🔗 Hybrid Cloud – Combines public & private clouds for flexibility.
🌍 Multi-Cloud – Uses multiple cloud providers to avoid dependency.

